{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_EthSwt_00455","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_EthSwt_00455@rel:R22-11#9fa0428e","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_EthSwt_00455","release":"R22-11","content":"{DRAFT} If an Ethernet switch has to elect an priority value for an received Ethernet frame, then the priority election process shall be performed according the following order: • If the Ethernet switch detect that the received Ethernet frame is handled by an per-stream filtering and policing (see EthSwtPSFP ) and the corresponding stream gate (see EthSwtStreamGate ) has an IPV configured, then this value shall be used as priority to map this Ethernet frame to a traffic class. Otherwise the Ethernet switch shall proceed as discribed within the next point. • Else if the Ethernet switch detect that a regenerated priority value (see EthSwt- PriorityRegeneration ) is available, then this value shall be used as priority to map this Ethernet frame to a traffic class. Otherwise the Ethernet switch shall proceed as discribed within the next point. • Else if neither a IPV nor a regenerated priority value is available, then the PCP of the received Ethernet frame shall be used as priority to map this Ethernet frame to a traffic class.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_SWS_EthernetSwitchDriver.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:13:22+00:00","cleaning":{"rule":"spec-text-clean@1","raw_sha256":"9fa0428ed1976692c850673f3a6099756062d1cfdf1fc0e7bd76029cd5c6983c","removed":["37 of 212 Document ID 656: AUTOSAR_SWS_EthernetSwitchDriver Specification of Ethernet Switch Driver AUTOSAR CP R22-11"]},"text_key":"393666bc55ba"},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_EthSwt_00455","release":"R23-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}}],"lifecycle":{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_EthSwt_00455","is_dropped":true,"first_active_release":"R22-11","last_active_release":"R23-11","d